{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GsyhtsGuwccafZg9ijqboR","type":"tool_result","content":"957b30bb chore(pose): bind the lres matrix to its review\n3f76982a chore(pose): index the lres matrix\n25413685 chore(pose): record the lres matrix\ndef347ab chore(pose): index the lres round r3 fixes\n761002d0 fix(pose): cut the quoted line, keep the reason; close only on a heading as written\n587e22f0 chore(pose): record review round 2 of the declared-limits residuals\n3c1bd90a chore(pose): index the lres binding\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-declared-limits-residuals.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-declared-limits-residuals.md\nindex d9a9cdb6..acdf9ac4 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-declared-limits-residuals.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-declared-limits-residuals.md\n@@ -110,6 +110,7 @@ Each requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n ### Execution log\n - 2026-11-28: R1 reads the heading's words with a comment removed (`isAcceptedLimitsHeading`); R2 reads inline code spans by run length (`insideCodeSpan`); R3 opens fences only up to three spaces of indent; R4 lets the next heading close the section whatever comment it holds, words the indented-heading problem and bounds problems to 20 plus a count; R5 the manual in both locales and the embedded copies; R6 refuses an unsealed limit for any decision (`unsealedLimitBlockers`); R7 tests the checks themselves; R8 keeps the earlier derivation for comparison (D1) and removes `acceptedLimitsOf`. `TestAcceptedLimitsResiduals`, `TestNoAttestationNamesAnUnsealedLimit`, `TestAnEarlierWithinLimitDerivationStillMatches` and `TestTheChecksPrintWithinLimitFindings` fail with each guard mutated out.\n - 2026-11-28: review round 1 (rrn-5b302e25c07a005e) requested changes. N1: only a line that is an unindented heading as written, its `#` first and outside a comment, closes the section; one that reads as a heading only once a comment is removed stays inside and refuses. N2: each problem is bounded to 300 bytes. N3: `PreflightReviewAttestation` refuses an unsealed limit for any decision, so preview and write agree; the error says attestation, not approval. N8: stale comments fixed. `TestAHeadingRevealedByACommentDoesNotCloseTheSection`, `TestAcceptedLimitProblemsAreBoundedInSize` and `TestThePreviewRefusesAnUnsealedLimitForAnyDecision` fail with each guard mutated out. N4–N7 are follow-ups.\n+- 2026-11-28: review round 2 (rrn-ada6c020a5ba9def) requested changes. N10: the quoted line is cut at 160 bytes, never the reason after it, and a whole problem at 600; the size test now requires the reasons to survive and fails with the quote cut removed. N9: the next heading must be a heading as written too (its raw line an unindented `#` heading). N11: `PreflightReviewAttestation`'s comment describes both decisions.\n \n ### Results summary\n The full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\nindex 2f8db5ee..cd6a0d77 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\n@@ -75,7 +75,9 @@ func ParseAcceptedLimits(body string) ([]ReviewAcceptedLimit, []string) {\n \t}\n \tvar entries []entry\n \treport := func(line, why string) {\n-\t\tproblems = append(problems, \"accepted limits: \"+quoteLedgerText(strings.TrimSpace(line))+\" \"+why)\n+\t\t// The quoted line is cut, never the reason after it (review round 2,\n+\t\t// N10).\n+\t\tproblems = append(problems, \"accepted limits: \"+quoteLedgerText(TruncateUTF8(strings.TrimSpace(line), acceptedLimitQuoteBytes))+\" \"+why)\n \t\tif len(entries) > 0 && !entries[len(entries)-1].bad {\n \t\t\tentries[len(entries)-1].bad = true\n \t\t}\n@@ -98,7 +100,7 @@ func ParseAcceptedLimits(body string) ([]ReviewAcceptedLimit, []string) {\n \t\t\t// first, is the next heading; one that reads as a heading only\n \t\t\t// once a comment is removed stays inside and refuses (review\n \t\t\t// round 1, N1).\n-\t\t\tif vis, still := visibleOutsideComments(raw, inComment); fence == \"\" && !inComment && strings.HasPrefix(raw, \"#\") && headingLine(vis) && !isAcceptedLimitsHeading(vis) {\n+\t\t\tif vis, still := visibleOutsideComments(raw, inComment); fence == \"\" && !inComment && strings.HasPrefix(raw, \"#\") && headingLine(raw) && headingLine(vis) && !isAcceptedLimitsHeading(vis) {\n \t\t\t\tin, inComment = false, still\n \t\t\t\tcontinue\n \t\t\t}\n@@ -191,16 +193,16 @@ func ParseAcceptedLimits(body string) ([]ReviewAcceptedLimit, []string) {\n \t\t\tcontinue\n \t\t}\n \t\tif seen[e.id] {\n-\t\t\tproblems = append(problems, \"accepted limit \"+e.id+\" is declared twice\")\n+\t\t\tproblems = append(problems, \"accepted limit \"+TruncateUTF8(e.id, 40)+\" is declared twice\")\n \t\t\tcontinue\n \t\t}\n \t\tseen[e.id] = true\n \t\tif e.bad {\n-\t\t\tproblems = append(problems, \"accepted limit \"+e.id+\" is not sealed: part of it could not be read\")\n+\t\t\tproblems = append(problems, \"accepted limit \"+TruncateUTF8(e.id, 40)+\" is not sealed: part of it could not be read\")\n \t\t\tcontinue\n \t\t}\n \t\tif !hasAcceptedLimitReason(e.text) {\n-\t\t\tproblems = append(problems, \"accepted limit \"+e.id+\" does not say why it is accepted ('Accepted because ...')\")\n+\t\t\tproblems = append(problems, \"accepted limit \"+TruncateUTF8(e.id, 40)+\" does not say why it is accepted ('Accepted because ...')\")\n \t\t\tcontinue\n \t\t}\n \t\tlimits = append(limits, ReviewAcceptedLimit{ID: e.id, Text: e.text})\n@@ -212,7 +214,8 @@ func ParseAcceptedLimits(body string) ([]ReviewAcceptedLimit, []string) {\n // acceptedLimitProblemBytes the size of each.\n const (\n \tacceptedLimitProblemLimit = 20\n-\tacceptedLimitProblemBytes = 300\n+\tacceptedLimitQuoteBytes   = 160\n+\tacceptedLimitProblemBytes = 600\n )\n \n // boundProblems keeps the first 