{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChUiffZUkVegGWgXYZTuz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WWzeyb3WnHnvgnUVrw98KL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"printf '%s\\n' '```pose-draft' '{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"approved\",' '\"findings\":[' '{\"id\":\"N12\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":225,\"summary\":\"Carries R1-N4: a heading \\\"### Accepted --> limits\\\", or a comment opened in the heading words and closed on the next line, yields no limits and no problem (R1 edge). No limit is sealed, so nothing is excluded from review.\",\"action\":\"Refuse such a heading, as the open spec follow-up states.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-28\"},' '{\"id\":\"N13\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":124,\"summary\":\"Carries R1-N5: indent counts characters, so a tab-indented (or two spaces plus tab) backtick block opens a fence that silently hides a later accepted limits section.\",\"action\":\"Count a tab to the next multiple of four, as the open spec follow-up states.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-28\"},' '{\"id\":\"N14\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":129,\"summary\":\"Carries R1-N6: a fence nested in a list item at four spaces is not read as a fence, so a comment opener in it refuses every limit. A further case of the same cause is silent: when such a fence is closed at two spaces, the closer opens a fence that hides the later section with no problem, where the base parser sealed L1.\",\"action\":\"Read list-nested fences, covering the shallower closer, or record the changed answer as a decision.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-28\"},' '{\"id\":\"N15\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":129,\"summary\":\"Inside the section, a four-space fenced block under a limit is now sealed as flattened limit text with no problem; the base parser reported the fence and left the limit unsealed. Nothing is cut, but it departs from the rule in the parser comment and the manual that other content is reported, and no spec decision records it.\",\"action\":\"Report a fence line under a limit, or record the changed answer as a decision.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-28\"},' '{\"id\":\"N16\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\".pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-declared-limits-residuals.md\",\"line\":128,\"summary\":\"Known gaps says None and Residual risks (line 142) says none beyond the origin spec, while the same report lists four open parser follow-ups.\",\"action\":\"State the open gaps in both sections at closeout.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-28\"}' '],' '\"prior_findings\":[' '{\"id\":\"R1-N4\",\"status\":\"superseded\",\"evidence\":\"Still reproduces in the overlay probe (stray close marker and two-line heading comment: 0 limits, no problem); carried as N12.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R1-N5\",\"status\":\"superseded\",\"evidence\":\"Still reproduces in the overlay probe (tab and space-tab blocks: 0 limits, no problem); carried as N13.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R1-N6\",\"status\":\"superseded\",\"evidence\":\"Still reproduces in the overlay probe (list-nested fence refuses as unterminated); carried as N14.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R2-N9\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"accepted_limits.go:103 now also requires headingLine(raw); the overlay probe refuses both glued-hash lines with the comment-marker problem, and TestAHeadingRevealedByACommentDoesNotCloseTheSection covers them and passes.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R2-N10\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"accepted_limits.go:80 cuts only the quoted line at 160 bytes; the overlay probe shows every refusal reason intact for long malformed bullet, prose, nested list, indented heading and fence lines, longest problem 298 bytes; TestAcceptedLimitProblemsAreBoundedInSize asserts the reasons and passes.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R2-N11\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"git diff 7ee50f0b..957b30bb: the PreflightReviewAttestation comment at review_bundle.go:3186 now describes approving and other decisions.\"}' '],' '\"sweep\":\"Swept the whole subject at 957b30bb: the round 3 diff; the accepted limits parser probed against the base parser for heading and comment variants, long refusals, heading gaps, tab and list-nested fences inside and outside the section; every spec under .pose/specs parsed by both with no differing limits or problems; the CLI preview and apply for an unsealed limit and for an open finding; the preflight and writer; manual copies; spec decisions, follow-ups and report sections. Run conclusion derivation and checks output are unchanged since round 1 and their focused tests pass. Ran focused tests, go vet of the two packages and the planned pose tools other than validate and the two post-review gates.\",' '\"criteria\":[' '{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Verified by probe: repository specs keep identical limits and problems, and preview and apply agree on an unsealed limit. The multi-line code span risk is stated truthfully in the spec. Unresolved parser assumptions are carried as low risks N12-N15, and the report wording as N16. The mutation claims of the execution log were not re-verified.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Parsing and admission logic only; no new shared state or lifecycle.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/mcp-review-attest-integration\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Refusals are bounded in number and size and keep their reason.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-approval-domain-preflight-integration\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Refusal reasons survive the bound; the silent edge cases are the low risks N12-N14.\"},' '{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Compared base and new parser over every repository spec: no difference. A non-approving attestation with an open finding previews and records successfully. R6 is the declared API change and D1 keeps earlier run-backed records matching; parser behaviour changes on unusual Markdown are carried as N14 and N15.\"},' '{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Focused tests passed here; no probed case seals a cut limit.\"},' '{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Examined each change against its cause: run-length span reading for R2, a three-space fence bound for R3, a heading-as-written guard and quote-level truncation for R4, one shared unsealed-limit check in preflight and writer for R6, and the comparison-only legacy derivation of D1 for R8. The design delta reports no structural fact to map.\"},' '{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Read the manual wording changed in both locales and embedded copies against runtime behaviour: section and heading comment refusal and unterminated comment refusal hold, with the edge exceptions N12 and N15. The embedded copy differs from the root manual only by a block also absent from it at the base.\"},' '{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Examined refusal text: each probed refusal names the quoted line or limit and why, 